&lt;p&gt;Join University Life to learn about food insecurity in partnership with the &lt;a href="https://foodpantry.cssi.columbia.edu/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Center for Student Success and Interventions&amp;#39;s (CSSI) Food Pantry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; team. Food insecurity affects many individuals, often creating barriers to academic success, mental health, and overall stability.&amp;nbsp; Together we&amp;rsquo;ll learn about the wide prevalence of food insecurity among university students, explore resources within and around Columbia&amp;rsquo;s community, and discuss ways we can collectively reduce stigma.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Meet new peers, share a meal together, and spend time getting to know about the CSSI Food Pantry. You&amp;rsquo;ll leave with practical resources and discover ways to help build a more supportive campus community. All students are welcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Columbia Serves&lt;/strong&gt; series invites you to make a positive impact through meaningful service opportunities both on and off campus. Get involved, explore issues you care about, and make a difference in your community.&lt;/p&gt;
