&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R. Grant Rowe, MD, PhD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Dana-Farber Cancer Institute, Boston Children&amp;rsquo;s Hospital,&lt;br /&gt;
Harvard Medical School&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot;Mechanisms of Clonal Evolution in Bone Marrow Failure&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;This talk will focus on understanding the clinical significance of somatic mutations in the hematopoietic system in inherited bone marrow failure, with particular emphasis on Fanconi anemia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Host: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.cancer.columbia.edu/profile/sergei-doulatov-phd" target="_blank"&gt;Sergei Doulatov, PhD&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Associate Professor of Physiology and Cellular Biophysics&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This&amp;nbsp;workshop&amp;nbsp;helps&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;promote&amp;nbsp;safe&amp;nbsp;behaviors&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;positive&amp;nbsp;community&amp;nbsp;norms&amp;nbsp;around stimulant use.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
