&lt;h1&gt;Who Moves and Why: Climate Change, Displacement, the Search for Solutions&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As environmental change accelerates, millions of people around the world are being displaced from their homes &amp;mdash; and the systems designed to protect them are struggling to keep pace. This event, co-hosted with &lt;a href="https://www.climate.columbia.edu/earth-institute-hub"&gt;Columbia Climate School&amp;rsquo;s Earth Institute Hub&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://globalcenters.columbia.edu/mumbai"&gt;Columbia Global Center Mumbai&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href="https://globalcenters.columbia.edu/beijing"&gt;Columbia Global Center Beijing&lt;/a&gt;, brings together a panel of speakers drawn from academic research, civil society, and lived experience of displacement to examine the realities of climate-driven mobility. Who is moving and why? Where are current humanitarian and legal frameworks&amp;nbsp;falling short? What might more durable and equitable responses look like? The conversation is designed to move through the full arc of the issue &amp;mdash; from data and policy to what displacement looks and feels like on the ground &amp;mdash; and is open to Columbia students, faculty, staff, and members of the public.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Speakers&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.publichealth.columbia.edu/profile/wafaa-el-sadr-md"&gt;Wafaa El-Sadr&lt;/a&gt; (Opening Remarks), Executive Vice President, Columbia Global&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://people.climate.columbia.edu/users/profile/alexander-de-sherbinin"&gt;Alex de Sherbinin&lt;/a&gt; (Moderator), Director, Earth Institute Hub at Columbia Climate School&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://newyork-un.iom.int/director-iom-office-united-nations-new-york" target="_blank"&gt;P&amp;auml;r Liljert&lt;/a&gt;, Director, International Organization for Migration (IOM) Office, United Nations in New York&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.climate-refugees.org/amalitower"&gt;Amali Tower&lt;/a&gt;, Founder and Executive Director, Climate Refugees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://people.climate.columbia.edu/users/profile/radley-m-horton"&gt;Radley Horton&lt;/a&gt;, Professor, Columbia Climate School&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/camilleandre/"&gt;Camille Andre&lt;/a&gt;, Regional Lead, Violence Prevention and Response, Latin America, International Rescue Committee&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.newschool.edu/nssr/faculty/achilles-kallergis/"&gt;Achilles Kallergis&lt;/a&gt;, Senior Research Fellow, Director of Research and Practice, Zolberg Institute on Migration and Mobility, The New School for Social Research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
